Byte order in graphics code. The decomp reinterprets 4-byte RGBA structs
and big-endian display-list words through u32/u16 loads, which only give
the intended value on a big-endian CPU. On the little-endian host these
reads assemble the value explicitly (port_be16/port_be32, mkdd_port.h).
Data that tools/web_wasm/conv already converted to host order (BLO
corner colours, the SCRN name-table offset) is read natively instead.
J2DScreen.cpp also fixes the J2DMaterialFactory.h include case (case-
sensitive host file system) and returns private_set's result.

